v 3
d twinmatch: policy-twin selection by Mahalanobis distance
d
d twinmatch finds the comparison units that most resemble one
d treated unit on a set of covariates -- its "policy twins."
d It ranks every comparison unit by Mahalanobis distance to the
d treated unit, reports the k nearest, optionally stores every
d unit's distance in a new variable, and returns the twin ids
d and distances in r() for use in later commands.  A z-score
d (standardize) metric is available when covariate scales differ
d wildly, and singular covariance matrices are handled by
d dropping collinear columns with a warning.  Useful for small-N
d program evaluation: picking comparison districts, counties,
d campuses, or hospitals, or building a synthetic-control donor
d pool.  Requires Stata 16.0 or newer.  No dependencies.
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
